## OpenInference keeps Portkey trace records open while streams are read

Source: Arize AI / OpenInference — https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference/releases/tag/python-openinference-instrumentation-portkey-v0.1.30
Published: 2026-11-16
Channel: github

OpenInference supplies instrumentation that records AI operations for observability. Its Portkey integration fixes when a span, the record of one model operation, ends during a streamed response. Returning the stream from the request is not the end of reading its output.

First, the integration returns a proxy around the stream. The proxy then ends the span when the stream is read, closed or dropped, allowing the record to include streamed output, token counts and iteration errors. The linked change covers both the Portkey chunk generator and its OpenAI stream representation.

Why it matters: Portkey users can check completed trace records against consumed output and test early closure and iteration errors after upgrading.

